{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted","id":1537906,"title":"How many mortals to beat a starting exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-30T14:49:40-07:00","id":1537906,"title":"How many mortals to beat a starting exalted?","content":"I just started a new game of Exalted last night. We are playing first edition but with some house rules to make terrestrial exalted more viable in a mixed party and to allow us to use the Vampire 5E dice.<br /> <br /> So the party of five exalted went up against twelve mortal militia members (average dice pool around five). Despite having cover, the exalted got absolutely shot to pieces and went down to a man.<br /> <br /> The players insist I owe them an apology for sending them into an overwhelmingly difficult five on twelve encounter. I suspect the players \u201cglass canon\u201d builds played a part in it.<br /> <br /> Either way, this is not what I was expecting from Exalted!<br /> <br /> Any advice on how I can better calibrate challenges in the future so that we have more balanced combats? How many mortals is an exalted worth?<br /> <br /> Lemme know if you need extra info like builds or encounter specifics or house rules or what not.<br /> <br /> thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T15:20:37-07:00","id":1537908,"title":"","content":"A starting exalt can, theoretically, defeat thousands of unexalted mortals. But that is going to require the exalt play to their strengths and not engage the humans in the way the humans want to be engaged.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I would need to know more about the situation before assigning &quot;fault&quot;. For better calibrated combats I would suggest going with 3rd edition and dropping your home brew rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T17:23:46-07:00","id":1537913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537908#post1537908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting exalt can, theoretically, defeat thousands of unexalted mortals. But that is going to require the exalt play to their strengths and not engage the humans in the way the humans want to be engaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about something more straightforward? Like, what if you take a bog-standard starting Dawn Caste and put him in a cage much against a group of amateur fighters and local tough guys? How many mortals to take him down?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537908#post1537908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For better calibrated combats I would suggest going with 3rd edition and dropping your home brew rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third edition may be better balanced, but we are all lifelong World of Darkness veterans, and the idea of having to learn such a drastically different system isn't really appealing to anyone.<br /> <br /> As for house rules, in my experience house rules are a tool to increase game balance, not something that hurts it, but to do that I need to figure out what the baseline of an &quot;intended&quot; combat is going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T17:28:52-07:00","id":1537914,"title":"","content":"In addition to what Shadowcat said, 12 mortals with ~5 dice in their pools and nothing else going for them should be a small Battle Group, not twelve individual combatants.<br /> <br /> Action economy can get the better of even the Exalted. Battle Groups are there to both make things easier to run by only have &quot;one NPC&quot; to run in the fight instead of twelve, but also maintain the aesthetic of the Exalted being able to take on armies with their supernatural might.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Exalted 3e isn't some major departure from it's roots in the classic ST system. Combat is far more mechanically intense, but you're going to run into that with any edition of the game. There's enough to relearn that works different from the ST system that picking an edition for being closed to the 90s era rules doesn't make much sense; esp. if you've already gotten used to things like V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-30-2024, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T17:43:28-07:00","id":1537916,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I'm not too familiar with the First Edition rules, but for anybody who is I think it would be better to ask the question that was asked than tell a person they want a whole new thing.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the combat system can't have been completely unworkable.<br /> <br /> As for me, my suggestion would be that if they were glass cannons, there might have been options to stay out of range or out of sight that they overlooked.<br /> <br /> Either that or simply not really being built well to fight, which either suggests a different tone of campaign to play or needing to go back to the drawing board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-30-2024, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:19:39-07:00","id":1537919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537916#post1537916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either that or simply not really being built well to fight, which either suggests a different tone of campaign to play or needing to go back to the drawing board.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, they are actually built to do little else but fight; the problem (imo) is that they went all offense. Everyone has way high Strength, Dex, and Melee, Brawl, Archery skills, but very little stamina or armor. Likewise, all of their charms are offensive in nature, none of them defensive, not even a simple Ox-Body to be found.<br /> <br /> So, the fight starts, and by the time they activated all of their charms and ready to go, they are already full of arrows and badly hurting. Once they start swinging, they basically kill one mook with every attack (overkill actually) but they only manage to get in one round of attacks before they started dropping, and by the end the party only had 1 exalt standing against 8 militiamen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:33:12-07:00","id":1537920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537913#post1537913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about something more straightforward? Like, what if you take a bog-standard starting Dawn Caste and put him in a cage much against a group of amateur fighters and local tough guys? How many mortals to take him down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to vary greatly depending on edition, build, strategy, and everything else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> As for house rules, in my experience house rules are a tool to increase game balance, not something that hurts it, but to do that I need to figure out what the baseline of an &quot;intended&quot; combat is going to be. </div> </div> </div>In my experience people making house rules that then complain about TPKs in a scenario where there wasn't anything remotely threatening have a house rule problem, but c'est la vie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:35:14-07:00","id":1537922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537916#post1537916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm not too familiar with the First Edition rules, but for anybody who is I think it would be better to ask the question that was asked than tell a person they want a whole new thing.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the combat system can't have been completely unworkable.<br /> <br /> As for me, my suggestion would be that if they were glass cannons, there might have been options to stay out of range or out of sight that they overlooked.<br /> <br /> Either that or simply not really being built well to fight, which either suggests a different tone of campaign to play or needing to go back to the drawing board.</div> </div> </div> </div>They asked how to balance combat, that was answered, they, and seemingly you, just don't like the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T19:01:21-07:00","id":1537927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537920#post1537920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience people making house rules that then complain about TPKs in a scenario where there wasn't anything remotely threatening have a house rule problem, but c'est la vie.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like you have had bad experiences with house rules in the past and are looking for a scapegoat.<br /> <br /> In my experience virtually every table has house rules (even a game's authors often diverge from the rules as written for the needs of their own tables), so you aren't going to find a pure game. But even if house rules are universally bad, none of them had anything to do with the situation in my game. Or are you trying to claim that boosting other exalted's Essence pools to match those of Solars is going to somehow cause them to LOSE a fight against mortals? What sense does that make?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537920#post1537920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...TPKs in a scenario where there wasn't anything remotely threatening...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so now we are getting somewhere. So 12 mortal militiamen shouldn't be anything remotely threatening for 5 starting Exalted in a straight fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","user":"Talakeal","date":". 06-30-2024, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T19:36:58-07:00","id":1537930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537927#post1537927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like you have had bad experiences with house rules in the past and are looking for a scapegoat.<br /> <br /> In my experience virtually every table has house rules (even a game's authors often diverge from the rules as written for the needs of their own tables), so you aren't going to find a pure game. But even if house rules are universally bad, none of them had anything to do with the situation in my game. Or are you trying to claim that boosting other exalted's Essence pools to match those of solars is going to somehow cause them to LOSE a fight against mortals? What sence does that make?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, so now we are getting somewhere. So 12 mortal militiamen shouldn't be anything remotely threatening for 5 starting Exalted in a straight fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>One combat focused Exalted is more like the four Chinese character compound \u4e00\u9a0e\u5f53\u5343, &quot;one worth a thousand&quot;. For starting characters, that might be a bit of an exaggeration, but after a bit of xp to round out a few areas, it gets a lot closer, and possibly exceeds it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T07:51:24-07:00","id":1537946,"title":"","content":"This has always been an issue with Exalted. What an 'average starting character' looks/plays like can vary wildly between individuals and groups. I remember a similar argument online in which one of the developers weighed in and listed off all the things they expected an 'average starting Exalt' to have, and thinking that was more combat-focused than the dedicated fighter type in my PC group. My memory of first edition was that the fluff text tended to create some unrealistic expectations about the baseline ability of an Exalt that may confuse a new player into thinking that they can be a hyper-competent badass without investing heavily in multiple Charm Trees and artifacts. A starting Exalt <i>can </i>defeat a dozen mortal warriors without breaking a sweat, but they have to be designed for it fairly carefully. <br /> <br /> I think you've correctly identified a major issue with your PCs lacking defensive abilities, but they may also have some gaps in their offense. Consider that a Terrestrial Circle sorcerer could easily take out a dozen militia with a single Death of Obsidian Butterflies while still being a glass cannon (though they would still need a plan to survive long enough to cast the spell, such as attacking from cover/concealment). <br /> <br /> There are a few things you could do short of just scrapping the existing PCs and writing up new ones:<br /> <br /> 1) tailor your encounters to encourage the PCs to fight in ways that play into their capabilities (i.e. put them into situations where the narrative suggests that they should be ambushing their opponents rather than engaging them head-on), while encouraging them to invest in Ox Body, Iron Kettle Body, Dipping Swallow Defense, etc. <br /> <br /> 2) have them go on a tomb raid where all the loot turns out to be defensive artifacts (armor, stealth gear, etc.)<br /> <br /> 3) throw them into some non-combat encounters, or encounters where they are going to be dealing with non-combatants who will be intimidated by their offensive abilities and not be able to exploit their lack of defenses. While encouraging them to invest in defenses and rewarding them with defensive gear. You may notice a theme.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while you don't want to penalize your players for designing the characters they want to play, it sounds like the core issue is that there's a disconnect between the character concepts in their heads (hypercompetent warriors) and what they've actually written on their character sheet (rookie warriors who have been seduced by the flashy attack powers and are learning the hard way that there's more to winning a fight than spin kicks and sword flourishes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","name":"Haerandir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T16:20:17-07:00","id":1537968,"title":"","content":"Okay so I think we'd need some knowledge on how things were altered with the homebrew stuff just in case we're missing something. Like to use a hypothetical porting 3e's mote regen per round into 2e would change things significantly. <br /> <br /> I also admit I'm not too sure about 1st edition's combat, but 2e's combat was described as rocket tag because of how important defensive abilities were to combat. From some of the stuff I found says1st edition actually had it where you had to decide to defend and it tended to consume your turn (as one success meant they hit and damage started in) in which case 12 enemies sounds like they'd be a fucking nightmare to avoid at all costs especially since apparently a hit would mean at least one damage since soak had a minimum of one damage get through I guess. <br /> <br /> Based on that I'd say lorewise 12 random militia shouldn't be that dangerous, the threat of a Wyld Hunt aside, but the way you described it your players decided to skip defensive options in the version of the game where getting attacked and still being able to attack on your turn meant soaking every hit that came your way until it was your turn if you didn't have a power that could defend you from the hits. So this sounds like bad builds unless things were changed by the homebrew things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Noticed the bit at the start where they said they used 1st edition with homebrew, edited to be more on topic. 07-02-2024, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T19:16:13-07:00","id":1537976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537927#post1537927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like you have had bad experiences with house rules in the past and are looking for a scapegoat.<br /> <br /> In my experience virtually every table has house rules (even a game's authors often diverge from the rules as written for the needs of their own tables), so you aren't going to find a pure game. But even if house rules are universally bad, none of them had anything to do with the situation in my game. Or are you trying to claim that boosting other exalted's Essence pools to match those of Solars is going to somehow cause them to LOSE a fight against mortals? What sense does that make?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you comment about changing dice to work like V5? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so now we are getting somewhere. So 12 mortal militiamen shouldn't be anything remotely threatening for 5 starting Exalted in a straight fight? </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be, but then again so much depends on builds and tactics. Your PCs should have won initiative and wiped out half the mortals before the humans ever got an attack. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T21:10:53-07:00","id":1537985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted#post1537906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just started a new game of Exalted last night. We are playing first edition but with some house rules to make terrestrial exalted more viable in a mixed party and to allow us to use the Vampire 5E dice.<br /> <br /> So the party of five exalted went up against twelve mortal militia members (average dice pool around five). Despite having cover, the exalted got absolutely shot to pieces and went down to a man.<br /> <br /> The players insist I owe them an apology for sending them into an overwhelmingly difficult five on twelve encounter. I suspect the players \u201cglass canon\u201d builds played a part in it.<br /> <br /> Either way, this is not what I was expecting from Exalted!<br /> <br /> Any advice on how I can better calibrate challenges in the future so that we have more balanced combats? How many mortals is an exalted worth?<br /> <br /> Lemme know if you need extra info like builds or encounter specifics or house rules or what not.<br /> <br /> thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>So like, what sort of Charms was the Exalted using? It's worth noting that, especially back in First Edition, an Exalt who isn't using Charms isn't mechanically much different from a mortal. A Dex5/Melee5 Dawn Caste can very reasonably get his shit kicked in by a Dex5/Melee5 Mortal if the Exalted isn't spending Essence or using Charms. <br /> <br /> A Solar Exalt with 2 Dex and 3 Melee, even using Charms to maximize their dice pool, could find themself in a tough situation against a Dex5/Melee5 mortal. That Solar Exalt can double their dice pool from 5 to 10 dice... but the mortal they're fighting also has a 10 dice pool, so you're looking at a roughly 50%/50% chance to winning (barring other Charms, Artifacts, etc). One of the unstated ideas in Exalted is that player characters should probably have fairly high natural dice pools, and then use Charms to increase their capabilities even further. <br /> <br /> An Exalt who, through the use of Charms and/or Artifact Armor can put their soak so high that it's impossible for a mortal to damage them could defeat dozens of people. Or an Exalt who could get their persistent defensive dice pool so high that (barring really bad luck on their dice rolls) are impossible for enemies to connect with. It's also possible for a Solar Archer to kill a ton of people by killing them from a range where nobody can hit the Solar back. But an Exalt, especially one who doesn't naturally have high combat stats, that tries to rush in and kill highly skilled mortals (or mortals who are good at using various tactics) without utilizing Charms or Artifacts is probably going to die.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm going to guess off-hand that the player was not utilizing their array of tools, or didn't build their character to be strongly defensive (you said they're a &quot;glass canon&quot;) and got trashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T22:33:50-07:00","id":1537986,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/TheErrataMaybe\" target=\"_blank\">This piece of commentary</a> by the first edition developer might shed some light on the expectations of combat in 1e. Mind the complete disregard for combo rules that even the official writers had, it was kind of a thing that brought us to the modern day where the combo structure of 1e got scrapped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T02:11:08-07:00","id":1537990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537922#post1537922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They asked how to balance combat, that was answered, they, and seemingly you, just don't like the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed yes, much like I would dislike a question about good vegetarian recipes being answered with &quot;have you considered how delicious steak is&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T04:29:15-07:00","id":1537992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537968#post1537968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on that I'd say lorewise 12 random militia shouldn't be that dangerous, the threat of a Wyld Hunt aside, but the way you described it your players decided to skip defensive options in the version of the game where getting attacked and still being able to attack on your turn meant soaking every hit that came your way until it was your turn if you didn't have a power that could defend you from the hits. So this sounds like bad builds unless things were changed by the homebrew things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not knowing the meta of a given edition is certainly a problem. 1e is all about getting a persistent defense Charm ASAP, and activating it ASAP, since persistent defenses let you roll your full defense against every attack without interfering with your normal options (like powering on other Charms, or not bothering because why do you need them against normal mortal soldiers?). Of course, people generally hated 1e combat because persistent defenses completely bifurcate the &quot;scale&quot; of threats. Things that have persistent defenses are basically a separate league from those without.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537990#post1537990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed yes, much like I would dislike a question about good vegetarian recipes being answered with &quot;have you considered how delicious steak is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, from a different perspective, the question sounds a lot more like, &quot;What's a good vegetarian recipe that can perfectly replicate the finest steaks in the world?&quot; Where, however dismissive and flippant, &quot;have you considered just eating steak if you want steak?&quot; isn't as off as a response. Asking about combat balance in Exalted, or even more so a specific edition of Exalted, and even more so further with house rules in play, is a lot narrower than &quot;generic vegetarian recipes.&quot; That's a lot more context and details involved that can lead to impasses were different desires become irreconcilable. The likelihood of an impasse only goes up if you also eliminate every vegetarian food options introduced within the last 15 years because people have continued to try to expand culinary options... just like Exalted designers have tried to continually iterate on the systems to try to get a better game for what Exalted is trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-02-2024, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T05:52:52-07:00","id":1537993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537990#post1537990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed yes, much like I would dislike a question about good vegetarian recipes being answered with &quot;have you considered how delicious steak is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an important difference, &quot;eat a steak&quot; doesn't answer the question, &quot;play a more balanced system without tons of house rules&quot; does answer &quot;how do I balance combat.&quot; I'm sorry you can't seem to grasp that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T20:37:10-07:00","id":1538020,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Let's try to avoid being outright rude and snarky to one another, please. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T23:54:59-07:00","id":1538028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537992#post1537992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not knowing the meta of a given edition is certainly a problem. 1e is all about getting a persistent defense Charm ASAP, and activating it ASAP, since persistent defenses let you roll your full defense against every attack without interfering with your normal options (like powering on other Charms, or not bothering because why do you need them against normal mortal soldiers?). Of course, people generally hated 1e combat because persistent defenses completely bifurcate the &quot;scale&quot; of threats. Things that have persistent defenses are basically a separate league from those without.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>So my limited understanding was accurate then? This was a fight of possibly some challenge or threat, but elevated to TPK nightmare due to bad builds for the system. (Assuming no combat modifications came from the Vampire 5 houserule stuff.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T13:47:42-07:00","id":1538054,"title":"","content":"The house rules mention was that they made Dragon-Blooded more viable. We know that the group &quot;used V5 dice&quot;, but we don't know if that means that rules from V5 were brought in or if it just means that the literal dice that they used were some kind of V5 set (in which case you're going to need a lot of them, this game uses a lot of dice!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T14:54:32-07:00","id":1538058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538028#post1538028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So my limited understanding was accurate then? This was a fight of possibly some challenge or threat, but elevated to TPK nightmare due to bad builds for the system. (Assuming no combat modifications came from the Vampire 5 houserule stuff.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In part at least? There's more variables and we don't have a lot of information to go on (hell the OP hasn't stated if they're using pre- or post-Power Combat era 1e rules).<br /> <br /> There's a lot to &quot;builds&quot; beyond Charm selection. There's lots of things that have been brought up like if the PCs were playing to their strengths. If you have five offense heavy combat Exalted in 1e rules... they really should be able to wipe the floor with a dozen mook soldiers before the soldiers even go. The PCs should have far superior initiative, and large offensive dice-pools that can allow for 2-3 (if not way more if they really min-maxed for offense) attacks each without activating any Charms that will still hit for significant damage as it is. If you make a character who's primary defense is overwhelming offense... you need to get on the offense before you get attacked.<br /> <br /> IME this sort of TPK is rarely something easily distilled to just one or two factors. It's usually a confluence of a lot of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T12:53:28-07:00","id":1538094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537993#post1537993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an important difference, &quot;eat a steak&quot; doesn't answer the question, &quot;play a more balanced system without tons of house rules&quot; does answer &quot;how do I balance combat.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How do I balance combat <b>in the game I am currently playing</b>?&quot;<br /> <br /> You've left out an important caveat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T14:38:12-07:00","id":1538098,"title":"","content":"So, after having read the responses in this thread and others, and also having reread the &quot;Make Sure Your Character Can Survive&quot; sidebar in the core book, in seems like I was more or less correct in my initial assumption, although I will still be looking at and potentially tweaking things. Thanks everyone!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538054#post1538054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The house rules mention was that they made Dragon-Blooded more viable. We know that the group &quot;used V5 dice&quot;, but we don't know if that means that rules from V5 were brought in or if it just means that the literal dice that they used were some kind of V5 set (in which case you're going to need a lot of them, this game uses a lot of dice!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am counting all types of Exalted as &quot;Solar circle&quot; for the purposes of things like starting dots, sorcery, Essence totals and Essence recovery to make them more viable (we are running a mixed circle of Terrestrial, Celestial, and Solar types).<br /> <br /> <br /> We are also using Hunger dice (yes a lot of them!). The four ankhs count as one success each, the fancy ankh counts as two successes, and the teeth subtract a success.<br /> <br /> Mathematically it works out to the same average of .5 successes per dice as standard Exalted's 1 success on 7-9 and 2 successes on a 10,<br /> <br /> While there might be some slight differences in distribution if you look at it using advanced math, that shouldn't be enough to cause something this major.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am also thinking of making dodge / parry automatic as I am told that is a very common house rule and one that greatly diminishes the sort of the thing we just had, but I haven't done it yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1537922#post1537922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They asked how to balance combat, that was answered, they, and seemingly you, just don't like the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you did not answer the question I asked (how many mortals to beat a starting Exalt) you did give an answer which could be inferred from my post.<br /> <br /> The thing is, even if I were playing 3E with no house rules, I would still need a baseline to calibrate my encounter design against.<br /> <br /> So in this case, the PCs got their butts kicked by a squad of mortal militia.<br /> <br /> My players posit that this is because such a force is overwhelmingly powerful for starting Exalts.<br /> I posit that investing in all offensive charms (and ones that took time to activate at that) meant that they were too fragile to win.<br /> You posit that my house rules are screwing with things.<br /> <br /> To test any of these hypothesis, I need some sort of a baseline. I need to know what a &quot;reasonable encounter&quot; is before I can even begin trying to work toward it.<br /> <br /> It's like trying to balance an equation with variables on both sides (Say 9 + X = Y), it just can't be done, the best you can do it move the numbers around a bit and make X = Y-9.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for house rules, it's a bit of a tangent, but IMO they generally make for better games. Clearly you disagree, and have probably had some experience with bad house rules (Celestines know there are plenty of them out there!).<br /> <br /> But generally, games are published by a small group under harsh time deadlines with plenty of compromises made and restrictions placed on them by corporate elements.<br /> <br /> Over time, the game's flaws will become apparent to the wider community, and common house rules will develop which fix legitimate issues.<br /> <br /> For example, giving everyone one free Dodge a turn is a very common house rule in response to the rocket-tag nature of 1E Exalted, and implementing it here would go a long way toward fixing the issues I encountered.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, of course, there is also the specific needs of the game. For example, the game the developers were making was clearly &quot;Solars = better than you&quot; and so balancing the different types of Exalts was not a priority from them, quite the opposite. But I want to run a game with a mixed party where everyone is more or less &quot;equal but different&quot; in their contribution, so my house rules to boost dragon blooded can only improve the balance point <i>that I am shooting for.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T15:57:33-07:00","id":1538099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538094#post1538094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How do I balance combat <b>in the game I am currently playing</b>?&quot;<br /> <br /> You've left out an important caveat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A caveat that, as far as I can tell, you've added after the fact. The OP's questions posed did not have that in them. It can reasonably be inferred, but putting it in quotes isn't a great look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538098#post1538098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there might be some slight differences in distribution if you look at it using advanced math, that shouldn't be enough to cause something this major.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't impact the mortals anyway. It'll have some pretty drastic impacts on how well certain Charms function (esp. Sidereal and Abyssal ones). It also hurts the Exalted characters by making their dice-pools less reliable. For better or worse, Exalted tends to use huge dice-pools to express Exalted being able to kick mortal ass with ease. Bringing the 1s subtract successes back into the base rolling math means you're directly increasing the odds of &quot;fluke&quot; rolls showing up. The old &quot;1s subtract successes&quot; rule has been known since the early 90s to actually impact high dice-pools more than low ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am also thinking of making dodge / parry automatic as I am told that is a very common house rule and one that greatly diminishes the sort of the thing we just had, but I haven't done it yet. </div> </div> </div>Taking you one step farther away from the WoD games and towards later Exalted editions anyway...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, even if I were playing 3E with no house rules, I would still need a baseline to calibrate my encounter design against. </div> </div> </div>Regardless of how one feels about house rules broadly, this is where I find myself agreeing with Shadowcatx: you're house ruling a game you and your players clearly don't know well enough to make effective house rules for. Adding in house rules before you even get the basics of the system is a recipe for bad ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My players posit that this is because such a force is overwhelmingly powerful for starting Exalts.<br /> I posit that investing in all offensive charms (and ones that took time to activate at that) meant that they were too fragile to win.<br /> You posit that my house rules are screwing with things. </div> </div> </div>We're positing far more than it just being the house rules. The house rules just make it harder to diagnosis the problem and even start to address the question of encounter design in Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tactics&quot; is still probably a huge problem that no amount of rules, RAW or house, can really account for. Milita, as stated in 1e under the Extras section, have a base init of 4, and 4 dice in combat pools, and are defeated with three damage.<br /> <br /> That's a very low bar for an Exalted to have to meet to one-shot them, meaning Exalted can one shot a lot of them without any serious risk by taking multiple actions,<br /> <br /> It might help if you actually detailed what your players and your NPCs did mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To test any of these hypothesis, I need some sort of a baseline. I need to know what a &quot;reasonable encounter&quot; is before I can even begin trying to work toward it. </div> </div> </div>Exalted (any edition) is too complex for this to be a simple undertaking. Exalted isn't a class/level system where you can set a reasonable idea of what an &quot;average&quot; &quot;level 1&quot; Dawn Melee specialist looks like.<br /> <br /> This is a game where white-room fights are also not super informative because there are considerations that are meant to calculate into things. A Solar that can curbstomp an army of mortals can't necessarily afford to do so whenever they wish. Actions are meant to have consequences. If you're blowing all your WP and motes as a Solar to flex on mortals, you're supposed to be in trouble when the Wyld Hunt comes knocking. The PCs are supposed to be weighing risks like that on top of raw combat math.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like trying to balance an equation with variables on both sides (Say 9 + X = Y), it just can't be done, the best you can do it move the numbers around a bit and make X = Y-9. </div> </div> </div>Seems like a case in point for what I'm saying. You can't solve this with basic algebra. Broad mathematics is perfectly capable of addressing the infinite set here. In any game that allows a lot of character creation flexibility, you have to be willing to get into things like set theory instead of trying to solve basic algebra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Over time, the game's flaws will become apparent to the wider community, and common house rules will develop which fix legitimate issues. </div> </div> </div>New editions of a game are generally a collection of house rules meant to improve the game, just written by the paid folks of an official company instead of the broader fan community.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned already, you haven't even said if you're using vanilla 1e or Power Combat 1e (a whole set of combat rules changes that happened in the 1e Players Guide).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, giving everyone one free Dodge a turn is a very common house rule in response to the rocket-tag nature of 1E Exalted, and implementing it here would go a long way toward fixing the issues I encountered. </div> </div> </div>Not really. From the basic descriptions provided, one free Dodge isn't going to help against a large number of opponents if the PCs have shit defenses and decide to spend their first few actions standing around powering on Simple Charms instead of charging in with multiple actions and Reflexive/Supplemental Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I want to run a game with a mixed party where everyone is more or less &quot;equal but different&quot; in their contribution, so my house rules to boost dragon blooded can only improve the balance point <i>that I am shooting for.</i> </div> </div> </div>Unless your house-rules only apply to the PCs.... that's not inherently true. The Dragonblooded outnumber the other Exalted by a few orders of magnitude. Boosting them to to Solar levels of baseline power just means the Realm and Wyld Hunt could easily crush a small band of enemy Exalted because they have more Exalted soldiers than you.<br /> <br /> Part of the balance of the game has always been that Solars might be the individually strongest Exalted, but they're one of the smallest in number and weakest at cooperation beyond basic mundane teamwork. Dragonblooded might be the weakest individually, but they're the strongest team players and they have the largest numbers to go with it. All the power the Solars have, and they all know that actually toppling the Realm is a feat they might never be able to pull off through their individual might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T18:09:03-07:00","id":1538106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538094#post1538094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;How do I balance combat <b>in the game I am currently playing</b>?&quot;<br /> <br /> You've left out an important caveat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And did I not recommend the game Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T02:06:20-07:00","id":1538112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538106#post1538106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And did I not recommend the game Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you understood I meant game as synonym for chronicle, table, session, group of players that have already created a bunch of characters with traits in a particular system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T02:09:26-07:00","id":1538113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538099#post1538099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">putting it in quotes isn't a great look.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to make great looks when being critical of a person whom I think not only took a bad attitude to how to answer the question, but doubled down on doing so in explicitly impolite fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T03:43:37-07:00","id":1538115,"title":"","content":"Sure it is... don't do it back at them.<br /> <br /> Nobody's forcing you to respond to ShadowcatX... you could debate the central premise of what I think i a shared position with me. Nobody is forcing you to be critical of another person over being critical of their posts (and I'm pretty sure the mods would rather use their powers in the opposite direction). Nobody's forcing you to make your points look worse because you're using low blows in response to bad argumentation. <br /> <br /> I certainly understand the impulse to chose to do so (<i>waves idly to his long posting history</i>) despite it not always being the best look, but even the OP has acknowledged that &quot;change editions&quot; might not be a desired response but is at least a logically valid response to one of the original questions posed; however it might have been expressed.<br /> <br /> So... what point are you even trying to make here? You're not defending the choice to stick to 1e as a good one in any meaningful way. You're not trying to address Talakeal's questions yourself beyond your first post in the thread. Am I wrong to presume you're trying to add to the topic(s) at hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T04:07:43-07:00","id":1538116,"title":"","content":"To keep this discussion about the topic rather than one another, I will just say that I think it behoves a good thread to maintain clarity about what an original poster's questions might be, and to identify points that might be unsatisfactory to them and even chase them off.<br /> <br /> I know I have experience of frustration with times that people were very much not answering the question that I asked.<br /> <br /> Now, I wonder if there's any mechanical heft to the First Edition system behind tactics such as trying to break an attacking enemy force down into smaller units that can be defeated in detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T06:16:55-07:00","id":1538128,"title":"","content":"Not specifically. War and official mass combat rules didn't really come into the game until 2e (not that there's nothing in 1e at all, but mechanical heft is lacking). 1e Core suffered a lot from not really thinking through where the game would go once characters got past &quot;You're a newly Exalted Solar, and you're still working on surviving the dangers of Creation,&quot; and the supplements were constantly playing catch up to cover things that the core just hand-waved or at best gave some advice on a one-and-done roll to see what happens. And that's not really just unit-level combat. Exalted 1e started as very freewheeling in how to handle anything outside of combat and sorcery: just pick a dice-pool and huck it was the general approach to most things. That's why the Exalted 1e quickstart basically spawned it's own fan-game that made the whole thing like that, rather that where the game went: trying to give every ability equal heft (still not there yet but a lot closer).<br /> <br /> Books like Savage Seas, Savant and Sorcerers, and Manacle and Coin expanded a lot of things, but if something you wanted more mechanical heft didn't become the focus of a supplement, it probably didn't get anything until 2e at the earliest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T13:24:50-07:00","id":1538177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538112#post1538112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure you understood I meant game as synonym for chronicle, table, session, group of players that have already created a bunch of characters with traits in a particular system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that interpretation never popped into my mind. I was thinking you meant different game as different edition. But in my defense their characters all died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T03:20:50-07:00","id":1538202,"title":"","content":"Specific advice to the OP: Combat in 1E is incredibly lethal. I've definitely played a Solar or two who didn't survive their first combat scene because I misjudged how many times I was going to get attacked. That's not even discussing Terrestrials, who never stop worrying about where they're going to get their next defensive roll.<br /> <br /> From what you've said about your group, I'm going to guess a lot of the PCs attacked early in the first round, using their only Charm of the round on offense. Maybe they dropped an enemy, maybe not, but either way, they had no defensive action to respond when another mortal took a swing at them. Even a mortal can seriously injure or kill an Exalt with a decent damage roll, and a dice pool of 5 will almost always hit a difficulty of 1.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a combat focused character, make sure you get a scene-length Charm that provides reflexive defense rolls in character creation, then activate it as quickly as possible in EVERY combat, mortals or not - good examples are the Solar Charms Flow Like Blood or Fivefold Bulwark Stance. Once you've got one of those up, you're defending against every incoming attack with a dice pool of 10ish, making it very unlikely that a 5 dice attack will sneak through. At that point, a starting Dawn could probably have soloed your 12 militia, though it would likely be a long and tedious slogfest.<br /> <br /> Even non-combat Exalts should invest in an instant reflexive defensive roll Charm - for Solars, those are Dipping Swallow Defense or Shadow Over Water. That lets you attack with your action and defend with repeated use of the defensive Charm as necessary.<br /> <br /> As a side note, crappy Charms are the true reason Terrestrials are always going to fall behind Solars in combat, not mote pool issues - from what I remember, they don't have a Charm like Flow Like Blood or Fivefold Bulwark, so even mortals will always be a threat. So you're going to need to house-rule some new Charms into their trees, if you want them to remain viable next to Celestials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 07-07-2024, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T11:35:38-07:00","id":1538208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538202#post1538202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, crappy Charms are the true reason Terrestrials are always going to fall behind Solars in combat, not mote pool issues - from what I remember, they don't have a Charm like Flow Like Blood or Fivefold Bulwark, so even mortals will always be a threat. So you're going to need to house-rule some new Charms into their trees, if you want them to remain viable next to Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah that sounds about right for problems with DBs, I remember 2e giving them a few charms that had caveats like &quot;Does not work against celestial exalts&quot; and the absence of those conditions being a thing I've been very happy about for 3rd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T15:12:32-07:00","id":1538216,"title":"","content":"While we are fairly new to Exalted, we are thirty year veterans of using the Storyteller System.<br /> <br /> <br /> While 7+ success and 6+ success with -1 on a 1 do have the same mathematical average, it is likely correct that they have distributions. I have enough statistics knowledge to brute force the answer by comparing every possible result, but that would take forever. Does have the math skills to actually map out the difference in distributions?<br /> <br /> I remember one time I was playing Warhammer and my opponent needed a 5+ on a d6 to hit, and he chose to rapid fire, which doubled his shots but gave him a -1 penalty, now needing 6s to hit. I asked why he bothered, as both were mathematically identical, and he acted like I was crazy and trying to cheat him. I asked online, and was told that it could be solved through binomials, and someone ran the math and said that while the average was indeed the same, the distribution worked out such that he is better off not rapid firing unless his target has more wounds than he could possibly inflict without rapid fire.<br /> <br /> I would be curious to see something like that here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538099#post1538099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned already, you haven't even said if you're using vanilla 1e or Power Combat 1e (a whole set of combat rules changes that happened in the 1e Players Guide).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not using Power Combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538099#post1538099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the balance of the game has always been that Solars might be the individually strongest Exalted, but they're one of the smallest in number and weakest at cooperation beyond basic mundane teamwork. Dragonblooded might be the weakest individually, but they're the strongest team players and they have the largest numbers to go with it. All the power the Solars have, and they all know that actually toppling the Realm is a feat they might never be able to pull off through their individual might.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is technically true, the population demographics of the setting are only tangentially related, at best, to what the players will actually come into conflict with over the course of the game.<br /> <br /> I noticed that the DB do seem a lot better are teamwork than the solars; I was hoping that would be enough to bridge the gap in play.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538202#post1538202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specific advice to the OP: Combat in 1E is incredibly lethal. I've definitely played a Solar or two who didn't survive their first combat scene because I misjudged how many times I was going to get attacked. That's not even discussing Terrestrials, who never stop worrying about where they're going to get their next defensive roll.<br /> <br /> From what you've said about your group, I'm going to guess a lot of the PCs attacked early in the first round, using their only Charm of the round on offense. Maybe they dropped an enemy, maybe not, but either way, they had no defensive action to respond when another mortal took a swing at them. Even a mortal can seriously injure or kill an Exalt with a decent damage roll, and a dice pool of 5 will almost always hit a difficulty of 1.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a combat focused character, make sure you get a scene-length Charm that provides reflexive defense rolls in character creation, then activate it as quickly as possible in EVERY combat, mortals or not - good examples are the Solar Charms Flow Like Blood or Fivefold Bulwark Stance. Once you've got one of those up, you're defending against every incoming attack with a dice pool of 10ish, making it very unlikely that a 5 dice attack will sneak through. At that point, a starting Dawn could probably have soloed your 12 militia, though it would likely be a long and tedious slogfest.<br /> <br /> Even non-combat Exalts should invest in an instant reflexive defensive roll Charm - for Solars, those are Dipping Swallow Defense or Shadow Over Water. That lets you attack with your action and defend with repeated use of the defensive Charm as necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more or less right, except even worse. Only one or two people won initiative, and most people didn't attack at all their first or even second turn, instead buffing, transforming, or conjuring weapons.<br /> <br /> Your post more or less sums up my assessment of the system,<br /> <br /> Of course, my players are kind of... stubborn. When I told them they might want to invest in defensive charms before they game, they assured me they would be fine because the best defense is a good offense. Then when the game played out exactly like I expected, they insisted that I would just throwing them up against &quot;an overwhelming force&quot; to try and make them look stupid for not agreeing with me about defense.<br /> <br /> Of course, without a &quot;standardized balance point&quot; for what this means either one could be correct.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... maybe I could send them up against a mirror match of the same party composition but with a more balanced distribution of offensive and defensive charms and attributes? But that seems a bit forced and belaboring the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538202#post1538202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, crappy Charms are the true reason Terrestrials are always going to fall behind Solars in combat, not mote pool issues - from what I remember, they don't have a Charm like Flow Like Blood or Fivefold Bulwark, so even mortals will always be a threat. So you're going to need to house-rule some new Charms into their trees, if you want them to remain viable next to Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> As I said above, DB seem better at teamwork than solars, so I hoped that might be enough.<br /> <br /> I was planning on home brewing a few defensive charms for DBs to even the playing field further, but my players told me no, they wanted to play the game &quot;honest&quot; and not have me home brewing stuff to help them survive. Which is odd because they are OK with my &quot;everyone is solar circle&quot; house rule and 5E dice we are already not playing the game vanilla, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T16:47:30-07:00","id":1538217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538216#post1538216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we are fairly new to Exalted, we are thirty year veterans of using the Storyteller System.</div> </div> </div> </div>IME, and a lot of people over the years have expressed the same, this isn't the positive it can feel like.<br /> <br /> Exalted, even 1e, isn't the same system as the WoD iterations, or the Aeon 1e iteration of the system (though closer there). A lot of mistakes get made when people are familiar with an old version of a system and don't really familiarize themselves with changes a new one implements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does have the math skills to actually map out the difference in distributions? </div> </div> </div>The -1 basically necessitates using brute force, even if normally through having a computer do it these days (since programing the function into something like AnyDice is a lot faster than brute forcing it by hand). Binomial distributions only really help when it comes to the odds of getting either a specific number of successes, or getting that number or more; not seeing the whole distribution over variable dice-pool size.<br /> <br /> I know a poster here named Ambrosia has the cWoD brute forced in a post in the forums... just look at the difficulty 6 column under the &quot;W. Specialty&quot; section to get 10s count as two successes. AnyDice has Exalted 2e's basic dice formula (which doesn't really change anything for this) as a function so you can display results over multiple dice-pools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While this is technically true, the population demographics of the setting are only tangentially related, at best, to what the players will actually come into conflict with over the course of the game. </div> </div> </div>Dragon-blooded tend to come up as antagonists... but it doesn't really address if your house rules are PC-only, or for all of the Exalted in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, without a &quot;standardized balance point&quot; for what this means either one could be correct. </div> </div> </div>You don't need a standardized balance point. They used bad tactics: if your defense is overwhelming offense... you can't sit around powering on Charms for a few turns and expect to be fine while people are attacking you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... maybe I could send them up against a mirror match of the same party composition but with a more balanced distribution of offensive and defensive charms and attributes? But that seems a bit forced and belaboring the point. </div> </div> </div>Probably. Though I have a feeling you could beat them without even changing their sheets and just fighting smarter.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think you have a group issue, not something some sort of hypothetical math problem can solve. It doesn't matter how well your D&amp;D edition is, if your wizard keeps trying to be a front-line DPS instead of spell casting, the fighter keeps setting traps instead of attacking anything, and the rogue keeps reading magical scrolls without knowing what they do. There's no house ruling that away. There's no &quot;baseline&quot; to figure out that will make designing fun encounters easier if your players ignore the mechanics anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T20:20:53-07:00","id":1538220,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded also get improved versions of the Artifact and Manse Backgrounds, as well as Command, so they would tend to be dripping with magical arms and armor, with an army on hand. That's the other counterbalance, especially in 1e, where how you paid for Artifacts through Background points made it considerably more difficult to start with Artifact weapons and armor as a Solar, renegade Abyssal, or Lunar (typically, it was one or the other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T10:58:39-07:00","id":1538241,"title":"","content":"My only advice is to treat Exalted as if it's a completely different system and yourself as a newbie storyteller in uncharted territory.<br /> <br /> I made the same mistake as you when I was first asked to run Exalted 20 or so years ago and I also thought &quot;I'm a veteran Vampire storyteller, I know this system like the back of my hand&quot;. I skimmed a few bits here and there and jumped straight to running it.<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;it's not rolled&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;what?&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;you asked me to roll for soak. It isn't rolled, it's automatic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hold up.<br /> There seem to be a few differences. Well, ok, but it's just that one bit, how different can it possibly-- *flips through the book*<br /> ...It isn't the same at all.<br /> <br /> Learn it.<br /> Doesn't matter which edition you pick up (I recommend 3rd, but that's me). Learn it.<br /> Trust me when I tell you that it's far less of an effort to learn the game and give it a chance RAW first than it is to basically write your own patchwork system and argue mathematics and statistics with people online.<br /> <br /> It'd also be less trouble for your players to do so than it is for them to face frustration and confusion like they did.<br /> <br /> Because let me tell you this:<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no way five exalts should ever lose to a dozen mortal average militia soldiers. None. Zero. I would be <i>shocked </i>if a single exalt lost to that. Like, you actually need to troll to get that to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T13:52:11-07:00","id":1538251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538241#post1538241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trust me when I tell you that it's far less of an effort to learn the game and give it a chance RAW first than it is to basically write your own patchwork system and argue mathematics and statistics with people online.<br /> <br /> It'd also be less trouble for your players to do so than it is for them to face frustration and confusion like they did.<br /> <br /> Because let me tell you this:<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no way five exalts should ever lose to a dozen mortal average militia soldiers. None. Zero. I would be <i>shocked </i>if a single exalt lost to that. Like, you actually need to troll to get that to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, arguing statistics online isn't a lot of work, I am doing it right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Aside from a couple house rules, I am doing my best to run it RAW. Although yeah, it is possible there are things that we just assumed work the way as WoD and don't realize it is different in Exalted.<br /> <br /> So, it comes down to the difference between 7+ success and 6+ success with 1s subtracting. Which, while they have the same average, do have a slightly different distribution, it is not the sort of thing that you are going to seeing over the course of one fight; just the random nature of dice rolls contributes far more than a minor change in distribution. Hell, the casting defects in individual dice or human error in counting up successes probably has as bigger impact over the course of a single fight.<br /> <br /> There is literally no way that this change alone can cause the level of disruption you are attributing to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T14:08:18-07:00","id":1538254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538251#post1538251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is literally no way that this change alone can cause the level of disruption you are attributing to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first of all, thank you for proving my point for me:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1's don't subtract successes in Exalted 1st edition.</span></b><br /> <br /> 1's only affect a roll if you rolled zero successes and rolled a 1 on any die. Otherwise they're just dud dice.<br /> <br /> Read the Rule of One on pg. 89 of Exalted (1e) core if you don't believe me.<br /> <br /> Like Heavy Arms said, and like I just said, your own veterancy in the system can work against you.<br /> <br /> Again, like I said, read the book like you've never read a Storytelling System book before.<br /> <br /> Fuck, it's probably good advice to read <i>any </i>RPG book like you've never read an RPG book before, because quite a few of them have some divergent core assumptions, small rule differences you can miss if you just assume you already know how they work and entire storyteller chapters that sometimes have unexpectedly great advice or present a different attitude towards this particular game in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T14:59:18-07:00","id":1538257,"title":"","content":"I've been in 1e games where over 300 dice have been rolled for <b>1 round</b> of combat. That fight lasted 6 of them.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is enough to see the differences in distributions to come up. And we were using a digital dice roller, even back then (OK, yeah, I do probably have that many d10s... but that's still a lot of dice) so human counting errors and physical manufacturing flaws weren't going to impact it (not that we were using house rules on dice rolling back then).<br /> <br /> Another one of those small rules that really makes a huge difference (though not one to the V5 dice choice)? Stunts are assigned to your whole turn. If you attack three times and defense twice, and get a +2 dice stunt out of it, you get +2 to each attack and defense, not just one of the rolls. The game rewards you for going over the top with your actions (and tells you this). I remember way back when a new group of people I was playing Exalted with thought Stunts were more like Willpower where you only get the bonus to one roll... which massively changes how the game plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T17:55:15-07:00","id":1538263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538254#post1538254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first of all, thank you for proving my point for me:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1's don't subtract successes in Exalted 1st edition.</span></b><br /> <br /> 1's only affect a roll if you rolled zero successes and rolled a 1 on any die. Otherwise they're just dud dice.<br /> <br /> Read the Rule of One on pg. 89 of Exalted (1e) core if you don't believe me.<br /> <br /> Like Heavy Arms said, and like I just said, your own veterancy in the system can work against you.<br /> <br /> Again, like I said, read the book like you've never read a Storytelling System book before.<br /> <br /> Fuck, it's probably good advice to read <i>any </i>RPG book like you've never read an RPG book before, because quite a few of them have some divergent core assumptions, small rule differences you can miss if you just assume you already know how they work and entire storyteller chapters that sometimes have unexpectedly great advice or present a different attitude towards this particular game in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry, one of us drastically lost the plot of the conversation.<br /> <br /> I said at the start that I am using two house rules:<br /> <br /> 1: All Exalts receive the same starting dots and Essence pools as Solars.<br /> <br /> 2: Rather than using standard Exalted dice which succeed on a 7-9 and count 10s as double success, we are using the Vampire 5 system where 1s subtract a success, 6-9 counts as one success, and 10s count as two successes.This has the same averages, but a slightly more random distribution.<br /> <br /> Shadowcat suggested that these house rules were what caused my PCs poor combat performance and that I wouldn't have seen it happened if I had played the game RAW.<br /> <br /> I was saying that this was absurd, as making dragon blooded stronger can't possibly make them more likely to *lose* a fight, and that the difference between the distributions of the two dice is so minuscule that there is no way it played a significant roll in the outcome of a single fight, indeed with such a small sample size just the random nature of dice themselves will drown out any difference in statistical distribution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:50:54-07:00","id":1538269,"title":"","content":"That's not how Vampire 5e dice work, either.<br /> <br /> And at least one part of your house rule is redundant, as 10s already count as two successes in Exalted. Which goes back to what I'm trying to get across here.<br /> <br /> As for the imbalance between different exalt splats, that's not something you can fix through Essence pools and starting stats. It has very little to do with either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:56:40-07:00","id":1538270,"title":"","content":"Just to roll back to this, as I'm a bit confused about how it was factoring in, how were you putting Hunger into a game where Exalted have no impetus to feed unless they're Abyssals, Hunger was meant to completely replace energy pools like your store of motes, and what were the consequences, if any, of Hunger dice replacing any other dice that the Exalted might be using?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T20:18:34-07:00","id":1538278,"title":"","content":"Yes, I am aware 10s already count as two successes. No, I am not implementing V5 rules or Hunger mechanics into the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only thing I am doing is having 6s be a success, and 1s subtract a success. <br /> <br /> <br /> I am doing this because it allows me to use Vampire 5 Hunger Dice because we have a whole bunch of them and my group has found it much easier to count symbols than it is to translate the numbers into successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T21:16:11-07:00","id":1538284,"title":"","content":"Alright, that's clear now. Did you allow the militia, who aren't heroic, to also count 10s as two successes? Because they shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T21:28:18-07:00","id":1538285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538263#post1538263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Rather than using standard Exalted dice which succeed on a 7-9 and count 10s as double success, we are using the Vampire 5 system where 1s subtract a success, 6-9 counts as one success, and 10s count as two successes.This has the same averages, but a slightly more random distribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... you mentioned most of the PCs losing Initiative against their opponents... how exactly did that happen? Because you can't use the default 1e initiative rules with V5 dice.<br /> <br /> Also, you haven't really addressed how things like Sidereal Charms are supposed to work (since their big shtick is changing target numbers instead of getting tons of dice).<br /> <br /> It might not be as easy on your group but even 1e Exalted makes use of the 1d10 in fashions a V5 specific die can't replicate; even more so the farther you get from the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadowcat suggested that these house rules were what caused my PCs poor combat performance and that I wouldn't have seen it happened if I had played the game RAW. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't the only thing suggested by ShadowcatX. Trying to paint it as the only issue at hand isn't really doing the conversation any justice either.<br /> <br /> And given a bunch of us have pointed this out, you could do with some acknowledgement of the fact that relying on lots of experience with other ST family games did not equate to an easy transition to Exalted if the party got TPKed on the first combat against foes the rest of us think should have been easily beaten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was saying that this was absurd, as making dragon blooded stronger can't possibly make them more likely to *lose* a fight,.. </div> </div> </div>You might want to remember the Anima Flux rules in a mixed group where the other Exalts are all glass cannons... because it actually can. The Dragonblooded don't have a lot of ways to make sure non-Dragonblooded friends don't get killed by their damaging Animas if they spend a lot of Essence. A DB that's at 16+ motes Anima Flux will eventually kill even Exalted around them if said Exalts don't have any soak enhancing powers that can nullify the 1 die of damage minimum. Doing ~1L damage to all of your teammates every 2 turns can be a problem for winning a fight (esp. a close fight that's already taxing the team).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T20:49:27-07:00","id":1538341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538284#post1538284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, that's clear now. Did you allow the militia, who aren't heroic, to also count 10s as two successes? Because they shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that rule? Because no, I was not aware of it, and yes, that could have made the fight more difficult (although it alone shouldn't account for it).<br /> <br /> The &quot;rule of ten&quot; section on page 90 says it applies to &quot;character's (and their opponents)&quot; but I don't see anything about it being Heroic only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538285#post1538285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... you mentioned most of the PCs losing Initiative against their opponents... how exactly did that happen? Because you can't use the default 1e initiative rules with V5 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>We used regular polyhedrals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538285#post1538285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you haven't really addressed how things like Sidereal Charms are supposed to work (since their big shtick is changing target numbers instead of getting tons of dice).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Don't know, hasn't come up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538285#post1538285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to remember the Anima Flux rules in a mixed group where the other Exalts are all glass cannons... because it actually can. The Dragonblooded don't have a lot of ways to make sure non-Dragonblooded friends don't get killed by their damaging Animas if they spend a lot of Essence. A DB that's at 16+ motes Anima Flux will eventually kill even Exalted around them if said Exalts don't have any soak enhancing powers that can nullify the 1 die of damage minimum. Doing ~1L damage to all of your teammates every 2 turns can be a problem for winning a fight (esp. a close fight that's already taxing the team).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I suppose that is possible, but none of them survived long enough for their anima to flare, let alone damaged one another with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T22:29:55-07:00","id":1538344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1537906-how-many-mortals-to-beat-a-starting-exalted?p=1538341#post1538341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's for Extras, aka any minor foe that's worth rolling against, but isn't really supposed to be a significant threat except in large numbers. Extras exist basically to get beaten up by Exalts without being a serious threat even if you can't completely ignore them (they're basically there for enemies to wear down enemies by throwing armies of weak foes at them, or for fresh PCs to feel powerful).<br /> <br /> Though here are other place where 10s don't count as successes in the rules (damage being another case)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We used regular polyhedrals. </div> </div> </div>So... you can see why it's hard to take the desire to use V5 dice over just using the normal rules if you're going back to traditional d10s for part of combat anyway?<br /> <br /> If you're really worried about quickly and reliably interpreting the dice, there are lots of dice rollers out there that can handle it. Onyx Path even has a dice-rolling app that you can put on your phone and shake to get it to &quot;roll&quot; if you want a visceral feeling rather than just hitting a digital button.<br /> <br /> Not that it would have changed anything if your players still decided to sit around turning on Charms... but it seems extremely off that they lost initiative that handily without a massively fluke set of rolls involved (or really bad builds on their part that would have been bad builds for a combat character in other ST-family games too; such as just ignoring Dex)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't know, hasn't come up. </div> </div> </div>OK... but since you know that it's a thing in the game... can you see why it seems like a weird thing to hold on to; esp. if you want to run a mixed-splat game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose that is possible, but none of them survived long enough for their anima to flare, let alone damaged one another with it. </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying everything here just to address that one fight. I'm mostly trying to illustrate that there's a lot more out there in the game that could come up that make some choices here feel like they're going to lead to more problems later.<br /> <br /> The larger point feeds back into the resistance to the idea of trying to set up some sort of mechanical &quot;baseline&quot; for fights. There's a <b>lot</b> in the game, and it's not stuff walled off behind lots of XP, or only available to a tiny number of characters in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}